# The Quota slice: the Militia line (Will Brack). The morning in the cells, and the road post from the
# post's side: the perpetrator's half of the pair "the requisition". Story lead, 2026-10-21.
# Slurs here are the invented ones (07-PRODUCTION decision 2 is open), each with a speaker who has a
# history (Gedge, see q_world.lwd) and someone who hears it.
# Weighted-devices pass, era 2, 2026-10-23 (design/DEVICE-AUDIT.md 3.3, design/device-audit/era2.md): no log, no
# order on the nail, no pass, no tally board. Tesk's oats are a half-empty sack by the cell door that Will folds
# over to stand like a full one (q.log_two) or leaves slumped (q.log_true); Holt says the order to the men's faces at
# dawn; the pole lifts for the faces the post knows; the sacks come off the cart by somebody's arms.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the morning in his trade
@node q.will.morning
place: q_cells
cost: 3
do: cut(max(0, 06:30 - clock))
nar: The cells, at the end of the night shift. Two lamps, one of them smoking. The smell of the bucket in the end cell and of Gedge's pipe.
nar: Will Brack has been awake since four. He has a heel of the post's bread in his pocket, from a cart yesterday, and he keeps putting his hand on it to see if it's still there.
line: GEDGE: Your tallowman's been singing again, sergeant. Half the night. That warbling they do. Like a sheep with its leg caught.
nar: In the end cell an old man in a felt coat sits on the bench with his hands between his knees. He looks up when he hears the word, and then down again.
nar: He's hot. You can smell it from the door, the fever smell, like wet straw left in a heap. There are lice in the seam of his blanket, grey, moving when the lamp moves, and Gedge won't go in to him.
line: TESK: I was not singing. I was saying the prayer for the water. We say it at night.
line: GEDGE: He says it was the prayer for the water.
line: WILL: Right. I heard him, lad.
voice: smell: The bucket, the pipe, and under both of them the fever, sweet and wet. It'll be in your coat by dinner. {dc: 3}
voice: grip: Your hand's on the bread again. {dc: 2}
nar: By the cell door, where the Captain will see them when he comes down at dawn, the two sacks the squad brought in from Tesk's fold on Tuesday. One stands up full. The other has slumped against the wall with its neck fallen in, half empty, oats showing at the top.
opt: "Fold the half-empty sack over so it stands like a full one." -> q.will.log.two {do: set(q.log_two); set(said.will_log_two)}
opt: "Leave it slumped where it is." -> q.will.log.true {do: set(q.log_true); set(q.true_in_hand); set(said.will_log_true)}
opt: "Ask Tesk what the oats were for." -> q.will.tesk

@node q.will.tesk
place: q_cells
speaker: TESK
cost: 3
line: TESK: For the goats, sergeant.
line: TESK: If the goats die, there is no milk, and then it is the children. We have six on the hill now that are not ours. Their people sent them up to us from the town. You know this. Your squad saw them.
line: GEDGE: Six little tallow-brats in one hut, and he wants us to believe there's no grain.
nar: Tesk looks at Gedge for a while, with no expression at all.
line: TESK: Your father drove Mr Orme's carts. I remember him. He would give the boy holding the horse a sweet.
line: GEDGE: Shut it.
nar: Gedge goes out into the yard. Through the door you can hear him kicking something until it breaks.
opt: "Fold the half-empty sack over so it stands like a full one." -> q.will.log.two {do: set(q.log_two); set(said.will_log_two)}
opt: "Leave it slumped where it is." -> q.will.log.true {do: set(q.log_true); set(q.true_in_hand); set(said.will_log_true)}

@node q.will.log.two
place: q_cells
cost: 2
nar: He folds the neck of the half sack down and over, twice, and tucks it under, and stands it up hard against the full one so it holds. Now there are two sacks by the door, the same height. The Captain likes things full. {sense: sack.drag}
voice: ballast: Half a sack. Nobody hangs for half a sack, either way. {dc: 3}
go: q.will.orders

@node q.will.log.true
place: q_cells
cost: 2
nar: He leaves it. It sits slumped against the wall with its neck fallen in, and anybody coming down the stairs will see it's half. He had his arm in it on Tuesday up to the elbow. There was nothing under the oats but more sack.
voice: pride: The Captain'll kick that over. He kicked the last one. {dc: 3}
go: q.will.orders

@node q.will.orders
place: q_cells
speaker: HOLT
cost: 2
nar: Holt comes down the stairs at dawn with his coat buttoned to the throat and stands at the bottom, where the men can all see him, and says the day's order to their faces. He says it the same every morning, in the same order, so nobody can say they didn't hear it.
line: HOLT: Nothing goes over the district line unless the post knows whose it is. Grain going over is hoarding. You take it at the post. Anybody argues, you hold them till I come.
line: HOLT: Two sacks off the hill. Good. That's a start. {when: has(q.log_two)}
nar: He puts his boot against the slumped sack and pushes, and it goes over, and the oats run out across the flags. {when: has(q.log_true), sense: grain.pour}
line: HOLT: Half a sack. That's what a sweep brings me now. {when: has(q.log_true)}
nar: He goes back up. Will heard it yesterday, and the day before, and he stands there till the Captain's boots are off the stairs anyway.
voice: ballast: If one cart goes through, forty go tomorrow, and then there's no post. There's just you on a road. {dc: 2, self: q.sl.forty_carts}
go: q.office

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the road post, from the post's side
@node q.will.post
place: q_post
cost: 5
do: cut(max(0, 14:00 - clock))
nar: The road post at the district line. A pole across the road, a whole young larch with a stone hung on the short end, a brazier, a hut. The wind comes over the plain from Osby with nothing to stop it.
nar: Will stands with his hands in his armpits. The chairmen's carts have gone through all day without stopping. The pole knows their horses. Gedge has been through every other cart since noon and found one sack, in a child's cot, under the child.
line: WILL: All afternoon. And one sack. Holt'll love that.
nar: A cart comes down the dip. A thin horse, a boy at its head. A woman on the bench, a girl standing in the back among the sacks. An older boy walking beside it with his cap pulled down, in a brown coat that comes to his shins.
line: GEDGE: Haldanes. From the barns.
line: GEDGE: That's the half-tallow one. Look at the wrist on him.
go: q.will.post.cart

@node q.will.post.cart
place: q_post
speaker: BET
cost: 5
line: WILL: Whose is it, missus?
line: BET: Ours. We're going to my sister's at Osby. For the mill there. Ours is shut, Sergeant, you know it's shut.
line: WILL: Then your sister comes for it, and I'll know her face. Off the cart, lad. Let the constable see.
nar: Gedge climbs up and starts pushing his bayonet into the sacks. The girl counts him. {sense: q.bayonet}
line: ANNI: One.
line: ANNI: Two.
line: GEDGE: Will you shut her up?
line: ANNI: Three. Four. You've had four.
line: GEDGE: What's in that one?
line: TOMAS: Barley. Seed. Same as the last time you asked.
line: GEDGE: Don't you get clever.
line: TOMAS: If I was clever I'd be in Osby.
nar: Gedge goes red from the collar up. Aaron, at the horse's head, laughs once through his nose and then looks at the ground.
line: TOMAS: The other two's seed, Sergeant. Barley. For the spring. Dad says if you take that there's no spring.
nar: Will knows the boy a little. He's seen him at the Sheaf, sent to fetch his dad home, sitting on the bench by the door till Ilo's ready. He has a laugh that makes other people laugh. He was laughing in there at dinner time.
voice: hearsay: Edie let Bet's dresses out for her that spring. The same spring young Furrowe got married in a hurry. {dc: 4}
voice: undertow: Two sacks of seed. Gedge is watching your hands. Whatever you do with them, he's the only one who'll ever know. {dc: 4}
go: q.will.post.choice

@node q.will.post.choice
place: q_post
cost: 0
# Holt comes because he heard Will on the square name the hill and the Hesh, in front of the Commissioner and the queue
# (a witnessed act, not the figure; author 2026-10-23, "Bookkeeping should not be a part of the plot").
alt: q.will.post.holt ? has(said.will_report_blamed)
opt: "Take the four off yourself. Leave the seed. Turn them round." -> q.will.post.take {do: q_cart = taken; set(said.will_take_four); shoulder(q.load.sack_light, 4)}
opt: "Put the four back. Lift the pole. Let them through to Osby." -> q.will.post.through {do: q_cart = through; set(said.will_let_through)}
opt: "Take all six. Grain going over is hoarding." -> q.will.post.six {do: q_cart = taken; set(said.will_take_six)}

@node q.will.post.holt
place: q_post
speaker: HOLT
cost: 4
nar: The Captain's motor car comes up behind the hut with its engine knocking. Holt gets out, buttoning his coat.
line: HOLT: Brack. You said it this morning, in front of the Commissioner. The rest's gone up the hill with the Hesh.
nar: He looks the boy up and down, the cap, the big coat, the wrist.
line: HOLT: Well. Here's one with his hill on him. And a mouth on him, I heard. Hold that one, Sergeant. We'll see who he's been carrying for.
line: TOMAS: I've not been up the hill since harvest. Ask anybody. Ask my sister. She'll tell you.
line: ANNI: He was with me. He was with me all the time.
voice: ballast: You said it. In front of all of them. This is just the rest of what you said. {dc: 2}
opt: "Take him by the arm." -> q.will.post.arrest {do: q_cart = arrested; set(q.tomas_held); fate(f.tomas_held, tomas); set(said.will_arrest_tomas)}
opt: "He's not been up the hill, Captain. I've had my eye on that road all month." -> q.will.post.refuse {do: q_cart = taken; set(said.will_refuse_holt); set(heard.holt.will_refuse_holt)}

@node q.will.post.arrest
place: q_post
cost: 3
do: record(refuse.pass, haldane, haldane_yard)
nar: Will takes him by the arm. Not hard. Tomas lets him. There's hardly anything inside the sleeve, the coat's that much too big, and Will lets go a little and then holds on again.
nar: The mother says the boy's name, just the once.
nar: Tomas climbs into the back of the Captain's car on his own. The step's high, and he needs both hands, and his cap comes off on the step. Will picks it up out of the frost, brown wool, warm still, and puts it on the boy's knee. Tomas doesn't put it on. {sense: q.cap.hold}
nar: The girl doesn't say anything. She's stopped counting.
line: GEDGE: That's one, sergeant.
go: q.dinner

@node q.will.post.refuse
place: q_post
speaker: HOLT
cost: 3
do: record(refuse.pass, haldane, haldane_yard)
line: HOLT: All month.
line: HOLT: Then take the cart, Sergeant. All of it. Somebody has to have been carrying for somebody.
nar: Gedge strips the cart, seed and all. The Captain watches it done, then gets back in the car without another word to anybody.
nar: Tomas walks back up the road beside the empty cart. He doesn't look round.
go: q.dinner

@node q.will.post.take
place: q_post
cost: 3
do: record(refuse.pass, haldane, haldane_yard); setdown(q.load.sack_light)
nar: Will climbs up and takes the four off himself, one on each shoulder, twice, and stacks them against the hut. They're light. Every one of them is half chaff, and he can feel it shift against his neck when he walks.
nar: The cart turns in the road. It takes a long time. The horse is weak, and the little one at its head won't let his mother use the whip.
line: AARON: Thank you for the seed.
nar: He says it the way he's been taught to say it, to anybody who gives him anything. Tomas cuffs him round the back of the head, not hard. Aaron doesn't cry, and Bet doesn't say anything to either of them.
go: q.dinner

@node q.will.post.through
place: q_post
speaker: GEDGE
cost: 3
line: GEDGE: You what?
line: WILL: Put 'em back, lad.
nar: Gedge puts the sacks back one at a time, slow, so the Haldanes can see him do it. Will puts his shoulder under the short end of the pole and lifts it himself. The cart goes through toward Osby and nobody on it says anything, in case he changes his mind. {sense: q.pole.lift}
line: GEDGE: That goes to the Captain, Sergeant. You know it does.
voice: grip: Your hand's on the bread again. {dc: 2}
go: q.dinner

@node q.will.post.six
place: q_post
cost: 3
do: record(refuse.pass, haldane, haldane_yard)
nar: Gedge has all six off and stacked against the hut, whistling while he does it. The seed goes on top.
nar: The mother gets down off the bench and walks to the hut and stands in front of Will, very close, and doesn't say anything at all, and after a while she gets back up on the cart.
line: TOMAS: Then there's no spring.
line: WILL: Order's the order.
go: q.dinner
